      <floats-group id="article-20378.s18">
        <fig id="article-20378.image.f2" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Kaposi Varicelliform Eruption in a Patient With Atopic Dermatitis. Kaposi varicelliform eruption, also known as eczema herpeticum, is a disseminated viral skin infection that occurs in patients with an underlying cutaneous disease. This condition is most commonly caused by the herpes simplex virus and presents with localized vesicular eruptions. Although uncommon, the condition can be potentially life-threatening if not treated promptly. Contributed by&#x000a0;O Chaigasame, MD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Kapsosi__Varicelliform" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
